{
  "_about": [
    "What each TLD is *for* — a topical A-Z, grouped by subject.",
    "",
    "Unlike the `categories` in tld-facts.json, nothing here is derived. There",
    "is no source that says .pizza is about food: the root zone records who runs",
    "a TLD, not what it means. So this file is hand-maintained, like",
    "eligibility.json, and it is our reading rather than anyone else's.",
    "",
    "Rules it is kept to:",
    "",
    "  * A TLD is listed only where the name plainly says what it is for. Where",
    "    it does not — .best, .now, .xyz, .zip, .one — it is left out. An",
    "    unclassified TLD is an honest gap; a guessed one is noise that reads",
    "    like a fact.",
    "  * Brand TLDs are left out wholesale. .apple is not a fruit TLD, and its",
    "    subject is its owner, which tld-facts.json already records.",
    "  * A TLD may sit in several categories. .kitchen is both food and home;",
    "    listing it twice is truer than picking one.",
    "  * Internationalised TLDs are keyed in punycode, like everywhere else in",
    "    this repo, with the label and its meaning in the comment beside them.",
    "",
    "scripts/harvest-tld-facts.mjs folds these in as `topics`, kept apart from",
    "the derived `categories` so a reader can always tell which is which.",
    "scripts/test-tld-facts-parse.mjs checks every TLD named here is real."
  ],
